From d22ce7949e56aed26b4aa1d46ab8b254336846eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:37:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 22/26] ipa: simple: agc: Support manual exposure time and
 analogue gain

Camera applications offer manual shutter speed and ISO, and an
exposure lock. Support ExposureTimeMode and AnalogueGainMode with
ExposureTime and AnalogueGain, and AeEnable, which sets both modes:

- the exposure time or gain set to manual stays at the application's
  value, clamped to the configured mode's limits, and the loop goes on
  with the other one (and digital gain);
- a mode switched to manual without a value holds the loop's last
  value, so AeEnable false locks the exposure;
- with both manual the loop is idle; a lock keeps the digital gain, so
  the picture holds, and the application's own values come without it.

ExposureTime and AnalogueGain are advertised with the range of the
mode the sensor is in when the camera is created; the simple pipeline
doesn't change the frame length, so the longest exposure is the
configured mode's frame time. Report both modes in metadata.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
